{
  "_doc": "Modules that resolve a data/ registry path themselves instead of calling gzkit.registries.load_registry (GHI #1067). SHRINK-ONLY: a module leaves by migrating to the seam, and a NEW direct reach fails closed. This roster is the mechanism that lets 30 readers migrate incrementally rather than in one unreviewable change -- it records where the parallel systems are, and refuses more of them. Presence here is not a defect in the module; there was nowhere to go before the seam existed. The first cut of the detector missed `Path(\"data\")` and rostered 30 of these 50 -- a 40% false-negative rate caught before landing; the corrected pattern is the one in gzkit.governance.trust_audits.config_derivation. Per ../airlineops/config/README.md principle 3, 'No Parallel Systems: one loader, one source of truth'; adopted by campaign Movement F.",
